===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q129}}The fifth day of the [[week]] in many religious traditions, and the fourth day of the week in systems using the ISO 8601 norm; it follows [[Wednesday]] and precedes [[Friday]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Romeo and Juliet Q1-2|act=III|scene=iv|page=53|passage=''Cap''[''ulet'']. {{...}} If vve ſhould reuell much, therefore vve vvill haue / Some halfe a dozen frends and make no more adoe. / But vvhat ſay you to '''Thurſday'''. / [[w:Count Paris|''Par''[''is'']]]. My Lorde I vviſhe that '''Thurſday''' vvere to morrovv.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1992|author=w:Toni Morrison|title=[[w:Jazz (novel)|Jazz]]|publisher=Vintage (2016)|page=50|passage=But for satisfaction pure and deep, for balance in pleasure and comfort, '''Thursday''' canʼt be beat.}}
